{"id":4,"titleZh":"什么让音乐具有交响性？","titleEn":"What Makes Music Symphonic?","date":"1958-12-13","dateZh":"1958 年 12 月 13 日","concepts":"音乐发展、变奏、模进、对位与卡农","thesis":"流行歌往往靠不断重复让你记住旋律，交响乐则靠对简短动机的持续变形、堆叠与对话推向高潮。","plain":"只用三个或四个音就能写出一整部大交响曲，核心技法叫“发展（Development）”：改变节奏和配器叫变奏，把短句一节节往高处推叫模进，多个声部一前一后追逐叫模仿与卡农，甚至能把原本完整的主题拆碎重组。","scenes":["伯恩斯坦先在钢琴上用猫王的《All Shook Up》示范旋律逐级升高的“模进”，再带领楼上楼下观众与乐队一起上演四声部卡农合唱《两只老虎》，还当场演示倒放与颠倒旋律。","奏完勃拉姆斯《第二交响曲》终曲片段后，拆出它把一条短小音型放慢拉长、退居下层伴奏甚至上下翻转的写法，再完整演出全乐章。"],"category":"基础乐理","bilibili":{"bvid":"BV1Gt411g7Yv","url":"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1Gt411g7Yv","title":"掘火中译：伯恩斯坦《年轻人的音乐会》| 什么让音乐有交响性？","duration":"59:29","uploader":"掘火档案（掘火中译）"},"scriptUrl":"https://leonardbernstein.com/lectures/television-scripts/young-peoples-concerts/what-makes-music-symphonic","repertoire":[{"composer":"Mozart","piece":"Symphony No. 41 in C Major, K. 551 (Jupiter)","titleZh":"第 41 交响曲“朱庇特”终曲","previewUrl":"https://audio-ssl.itunes.apple.com/itunes-assets/AudioPreview125/v4/80/1c/1d/801c1dc9-c14c-f5bf-7ca9-f39ad3325d4f/mzaf_1303989186037093550.plus.aac.p.m4a","appleMusicUrl":"https://music.apple.com/us/album/symphony-no-41-in-c-major-k-551-i-allegro-vivace/930644673?i=930644683&uo=4","recordingArtist":"Mozart Festival Orchestra & Richard Edlinger","recordingTrack":"Symphony No. 41 in C Major, K. 551: I. Allegro vivace","youtubeSearchUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Mozart%20Symphony%20No.%2041%20in%20C%20Major%2C%20K.%20551+Bernstein","biliSearchUrl":"https://search.bilibili.com/all?keyword=Mozart%20Symphony%20No.%2041%20in%20C%20Major%2C%20K.%20551"},{"composer":"Beethoven","piece":"Symphony No. 5 in C Minor, Op. 67","titleZh":"第五交响曲","previewUrl":"https://audio-ssl.itunes.apple.com/itunes-assets/AudioPreview221/v4/52/93/02/52930254-6025-c7d2-92cb-44f34e24c22d/mzaf_2193174951270121243.plus.aac.p.m4a","appleMusicUrl":"https://music.apple.com/us/album/symphony-no-5-in-c-minor-op-67-orch-by-gustav-mahler/1743941872?i=1743941874&uo=4","recordingArtist":